# Production release target

- This repository has one production product target: the private shared
  MultiImageClient image-making site the owner calls
  `multi-image-client-alpha.fuseki.net`.
- Its currently installed canonical DNS/TLS vhost is
  `multiimageclient.alpha.fuseki.net`. Treat the two names as the same intended
  product site; an ordinary deploy must not rename DNS, TLS, or nginx.
- `tpbeta` is only the colocated physical host. It is not the product/site
  identity, and its other services and vhosts are outside this repository's
  deployment scope.
- In this repository, “push and deploy” normally means: run CI, push the
  requested Git branch to GitHub, then re-release only
  `multiimageclient-ui.service` through `deploy/agent-redeploy.sh`.
- On this workstation, the `tpbeta` SSH alias logs in as `subcreation`, which
  does not own the checkout. Use the documented `tpbeta-root` command that
  runs the release as `tparkour`; never guess another checkout or service.
- Verify the exact commit, active service, fresh start time, loopback response,
  and private public vhost after deployment. Never print or disclose the
  site's secret path, credentials, cookies, or provider keys.
